      "width": 3216,
      "height": 2136,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Jorge Láscar from Australia",
      "description": "The Wangfujing Cathedral (王府井天主堂), also named St. Joseph's Wangfujing Cathedral or to the locals, Dongtang (东堂, the East Cathedral) is a historic Catholic  cathedral located in downtown Beijing, near the Wangfujing. A small church was first established in 1653 on the open grounds by the Jesuit Father Lodovico Buglio.  Later several earthquakes and wars gradually destroyed the church. It was rebuilt in 1904 as a Romanesque cathedral, with strong pilasters and one high and two low vaults displaying a grandiose architectural style. After the restoration in 1980, the church reopened. Because of its geographic location, the Church faces west.\n\nThe plaza in front of Wangfujing Cathedral is the most popular location for skateboarding in Beijing.",
      "dateCreated": "2008-11-26 14:09",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "st-joseph-s-church-beijing-wp",
